/*
# Lustre

Mobile detailing assistant powered by Gemini. Static PWA (`index.html`, `sw.js`, `manifest.webmanifest`) plus edge functions that keep your API key server-side: `api/chat` (streaming answers) and `api/tts` (Gemini voice).

## Deploy
1. Push this folder to GitHub.
2. In EdgeOne Pages, create a project from the repo (no build command, output directory = repo root).
3. Add env vars: `GEMINI_API_KEY` (required), `GEMINI_MODEL` (optional, default `gemini-2.5-flash`), `GEMINI_TTS_MODEL` (optional, default `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts`).
4. Redeploy. Open the site on your phone over HTTPS and use "Add to Home Screen" for the offline app.

## What's inside
- **New job wizard:** full-screen setup for vehicle, one or more services, condition, issues, optional photos, client and ETA. Runs on first launch and from Job > New job. Cancel leaves the current job untouched.
- **Job (home):** vehicle card with progress ring, multi-service picker (full exterior, paint correction, interior detail, interior deep clean, trim restoration, headlight restoration, maintenance wash, engine bay), combined checklist, progress tracker, site weather, shortcut tiles.
- **Ask:** streaming chat with typing effect and a stop button, voice input, photo/video attach, quick chips. Job context goes with every message.
- **Tools:** Mix (dilution calculator, presets), Timers (standard or large digits), Depth (multi-spot paint depth grid).
- **Kit:** chemicals with mix ratios, tools and equipment. Chemical entries can jump to the calculator.
- **Log:** inspection photos, notes, client text templates.
- **Audio:** Gemini voices with an automatic fallback to the best voice on the device. Pick them in Settings.

## Site version and update wall
The current version is shown under the Lustre title and in Settings. To ship an update, change `SITE_VERSION` near the top of the script in `index.html`, then add or edit the matching entry in `SITE_UPDATES` (newest first). The update wall opens automatically for returning users when the version changes, and is always available from Settings > What’s new. Bump the cache name in `sw.js` whenever you change the app shell.

## Multiple services
Select one or more services during setup or from the Job tab. Lustre merges shared stages (for example Wash or Correct) into one checklist and orders the remaining stages for the job. The package label, progress tracker, client texts and AI context all use the full service list.

## Paint depth
Each of the nine standard panels stores any number of readings for the current job in IndexedDB. The panel color comes from the lowest reading: safe above 110 µm, caution at 85–110 µm, danger below 85 µm. Units switch between microns and mils (1 mil = 25.4 µm).

## Alerts and timers
- Headphone alerts use native system notifications through the service worker. Enable them in Settings; the OS decides whether the sound routes to connected headphones.
- Larger timers make the digits glanceable from the bench.
- Timers and job alerts run while Lustre is open. Background delivery while the app is closed needs a push backend.
- The service worker and `/api/push/subscribe` hook are in place, but `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` in `index.html` is empty. Add a VAPID public key and a sender endpoint to enable server push.

## Hey Lustre
The wake word uses the browser SpeechRecognition API while Lustre is open. Say “Hey Lustre” and then a command. It pauses while the mic or a chat request is active. Browser speech recognition may need a connection, and it stops when the app is closed. Microphone access requires HTTPS and permission. If speech recognition is unsupported, use keyboard dictation or type instead.

On Android Chrome, hands-free listening can continue while Lustre stays open. iOS Safari and installed Home Screen apps may stop listening after a phrase or when the app goes to the background. Tap the wake badge or the mic button to restart. If the wake badge disappears, turn “Hey Lustre” back on in Settings.

Commands run locally first and fall back to the Gemini chat when Lustre does not recognize them. Examples:
- Job: “set vehicle to 2022 BMW M3”, “set client to Sam”, “set ETA to 3 PM”, “add note that trim needs dressing”, “add paint correction”, “remove trim restoration”, “next step”, “back a step”, “check foam dwell”, “what’s next”.
- Timers: “start a 5 minute dwell timer”, “cancel the cure timer”, “how much time is left”, “large timers on”.
- Depth and mix: “log 120 microns on the hood”, “add 4.5 mils to the driver’s door”, “paint depth status”, “switch depth to mils”, “calculate 1 to 10 for a 32 ounce bottle”.
- App: “open timers”, “open kit”, “show checklist”, “what’s the weather”, “turn on alerts”, “audio off”, “wake word on”, “what’s new”, “what version”, “help”.

Voice commands reuse the same job, checklist, timer, calculator, paint-depth and kit state as the touch UI. Enabling alerts by voice can still be limited by the browser’s notification permission prompt.

## iOS home screen
`apple-touch-icon.png` (180 px), `icon-192.png`, `icon-512.png` and `icon-maskable-512.png` are generated from the Lustre mark. In Safari, tap Share > Add to Home Screen to use it as the app icon.

## Offline
Everything except chat, Gemini voice, live weather and wake-word speech recognition works offline. Data lives on the device (localStorage and IndexedDB).

## Media in chat
Photos are resized in the browser. Videos are reduced to 8 frames to stay under edge payload limits.
*/
